  "body": "## What changed\n\n- New test file `crates/app/tests/lathe_post_g76_sources.rs`. It pins three G76 readings that two published manuals of two different makers settle.\n- The G76 fixture and the control model move from `lathe_post_g76_schedule.rs` to `crates/app/tests/common/g76.rs`. The schedule suite was at the 400-line limit. Its tests do not change.\n- Decision file `docs/decisions/1842-g76-schedule-sources.md` gives the sources and the readings.\n- The post, the goldens and the posted G-code do not change. This PR does not touch `assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps`. Thus no conflict with #1866 or #468 is expected.\n\n## Sources\n\n- S1: FANUC Series 0i-MODEL F Operator's Manual, Lathe System, B-64604EN-1/01, section 4.2.7 \"Multiple Threading Cycle (G76)\", Fig. 4.2.7 (a) and (b).\n- S2: Siemens SINUMERIK ISO Turning Programming Manual 07/2022, A5E52211627B AA, \"Multiple-thread cutting cycle (G76)\", Fig. 4-25 and 4-26, pages 87-89.\n- Contrast only: Hurco WinMax Lathe G76, Haas lathe G76, GSK988TA G76, LinuxCNC G76.\n\n## Readings\n\n1. Start point and Z shift: settled. The post agrees. The cycle starts at A above the crest point B. Each deeper pass starts `depth * tan(a/2)` further along the travel (one edge cuts).\n2. End point: settled. The post agrees. Every pass ends at the programmed end point D. The kernel lays shallower passes short of D. The control cuts them to D, inside the groove of the root pass. This removes no extra material. #1896 tracks the simulation detail.\n3. Minimum depth: settled. The post agrees. Q(dmin) clamps the cut of one pass below the pass before it.\n4. Internal rounding of `dd * sqrt(n)`: open. No source states it. The post's guard stays.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `lathe_post_g76_sources::each_pass_starts_on_the_crest_flank_line_along_the_travel`\n- `lathe_post_g76_sources::every_pass_runs_to_the_posted_end_z_inside_the_root_pass`\n- `lathe_post_g76_sources::the_minimum_depth_clamps_the_cut_of_one_pass` (it also proves that the other clamp reading gives a different ladder)\n\n## Gate\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test lathe_post_g76_schedule --test lathe_post_g76_sources`: 7 + 3 passed. The golden `thread_g76_area.nc` did not change.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test lathe_post_g76_schedule --test lathe_post_g76_sources -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No Fanuc control or simulator was available. No reading was run on a control.\n- Reading 4 stays open on #1842.\n- Clippy ran on the two touched test binaries only, not on `--all-targets`. The other app test binaries also compile `common/g76.rs`.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: high\n\nRefs #1842\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
